1
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:12,666
The amps are on but nobody's home.

2
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
Airheads is a comedy, crime, music film directed by Michael Lehmann.

3
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
The Lone Rangers have heavy-metal dreams and a single
demo tape they can't get anyone to play.

4
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
The solution: Hijack an FM rock radio station and hold the deejays
hostage until they agree to broadcast the band's tape.

5
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
Chester 'Chazz' Darvey, played by Brendan Fraser.

6
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Rex, played by Steve Buscemi.

7
00:35:46,666 --> 00:35:52,666
Pip, played by Adam Sandler.

8
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:59,333
Ian, played by Joe Mantegna.

9
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Officer Wilson, played by Chris Farley.

10
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Jimmie Wing, played by Judd Nelson.

11
00:56:13,333 --> 00:56:19,333
Airheads is a 1994 American comedy film directed by
Michael Lehmann and written by Rich Wilkes.

12
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
It stars Brendan Fraser, Steve Buscemi, and Adam Sandler as the members of a struggling rock
band who hijack a Los Angeles radio station in order to get their demo aired.

13
01:06:26,666 --> 01:06:32,666
The rest of the principal cast includes Chris Farley, Michael McKean, Judd Nelson, Michael Richards,
and Joe Mantegna, with Ernie Hudson, Amy Locane, Nina Siemaszko, Marshall Bell, Reg E.

14
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
Cathey, and David Arquette in supporting roles.

15
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
Airheads was a critical and commercial failure, but has
since come to be viewed as a cult film.

16
01:21:46,666 --> 01:21:52,666
The film explores themes of radio station, heavy metal, rock band.

17
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:59,333
The tone is lighthearted.
